WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.300
If the shoe fits...

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.300
wear it!

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.300
I take apart

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.300
the new Cinderella--

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.800
--on this week's episode of Angry Nerd!

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.390
First, your comments.

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:12.660
Rodney Funderburrk writes,

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:13.800
“Can you make a video”

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.170
“about whether books or movies”

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:16.760
“are better for franchises like”

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.970
“Harry Potter, Lord of the Rings,
and Twilight?”

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:19.990
Rodney, books and movies

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:21.869
are two different mediums,

00:00:21.869 --> 00:00:23.810
and each are good in there own ways!

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:25.480
Except for Twilight!

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:26.480
Twilight books and movies

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:27.480
are each BAD

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:28.480
in their own ways!

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:29.480
A live action version

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.500
of Disney's Cinderella

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:31.679
is coming out and...

00:00:31.679 --> 00:00:34.570
it's giving me a powerful sense of deja vu.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:35.640
I mean, there have been

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.140
THIRTEEN movie adaptations

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.480
of this story since 2000,

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:40.480
including Into the Woods

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.720
just a coupla months ago.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:42.720
I don't see what sets this

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.580
new Kenneth Branagh adaptation apart...

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.400
Except more plot machinations

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:47.550
with the wicked stepmother--

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:48.830
YAWN!

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:50.930
Why is Disney turning yet another

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:52.480
animated classic into live action?

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:55.110
Is it because Maleficent earned over $750
million?

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.110
I guess they--

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:59.640
Yeah, I figured that was the reason why.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:01.070
But I guess this new Cinderella

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:02.730
doesn't really have to reinvent the wheel,

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:04.890
because the 400 year-old storyline

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:08.080
is so durable and universally appealing.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:09.500
People naturally respond

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.970
to the downtrodden protagonist

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.470
whose special qualities are finally recognized.

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:14.781
I can guarantee you that

00:01:14.781 --> 00:01:16.460
they'll still be staging Cinderella

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.630
at outposts on Rigel 7

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:20.550
in the year 2395.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:21.890
A story with that sort of

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:24.750
timeless appeal is potent stuff.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.090
Seriously, has anybody in our lifetime

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:28.370
come up with a tale that we can

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:29.590
confidently predict

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:31.830
will still be in circulation

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:33.030
four centuries from now?

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.350
I would say…

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:35.350
George Lucas.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:37.479
Imean, the man has a lot to answer for,

00:01:37.479 --> 00:01:39.620
but in the pre-prequel era,

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.480
he really tapped into something primal.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.800
“I... am your father!”

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:45.800
“Noooooooo!”

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:46.800
Remember in Reign of Fire

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.060
when the adults stage Star Wars

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.170
for the kids?

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:51.409
“I... am your father!”

00:01:51.409 --> 00:01:52.409
“GASP!”

00:01:52.409 --> 00:01:55.380
That was the best scene in that postapocalyptic
dud.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:56.950
Who else's work will endure?

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.229
Stan Lee, maybe.

00:01:58.229 --> 00:01:59.869
Future generations will still wish

00:01:59.869 --> 00:02:01.549
they could be like the wallflower

00:02:01.549 --> 00:02:04.280
who gains extraordinary super powers.

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:06.570
They'll probably also think that 20th century
people

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:08.929
were all so gullible and superstitious

00:02:08.929 --> 00:02:12.010
that we really believed that radioactive arachnids

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:13.670
would actually have that effect!

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:15.540
I knew that that wasn't how science works,

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.130
people from the distant future!

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:18.480
Revive my cryofrozen head,

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.819
and I will explain our era to you.

00:02:20.819 --> 00:02:22.370
Who else stands the test of time?

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:23.370
Walt Disney?

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:24.370
Yeah.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:25.370
John Lasseter?

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:26.370
It's likely..

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:27.370
Dr. Seuss?

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:28.370
Natch.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:29.370
Shigeru Miyamoto?

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:30.370
Of course!

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:31.370
J. K. Rowling?

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:32.370
No--

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:33.370
they'll find the educational system

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:34.370
elitist and brutalizing.

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:35.370
Michael Bay?

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:36.370
Are you kidding?!

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:37.370
His stuff seems archaic NOW!

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:39.239
So Disney's doing a live action Cinderella
this year,

00:02:39.239 --> 00:02:40.660
and a live action Jungle Book

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:41.660
and Beauty and the Beast

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:42.910
are coming next year.

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:44.130
I mean what's next,

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:50.230
a live action Pirates of the Caribbean?!

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:51.230
What?

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:52.230
No, you're mistaken.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.390
See, it’s very sophisticated animatronics,

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:55.390
just like the ride.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:56.720
No, no, no,

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:00.290
because I read it in Variety, that’s--

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:02.200
not real people.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.280
I hate it when you go “Well...”

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.870
And then you tell me that I’m wrong

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.690
when I know that I’m right!

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:07.959
They’re animatronic robots!

00:03:07.959 --> 00:03:08.970
Nope, nope!

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:13.690
Well… we’ll agree to disagree.

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:15.239
I'm assuming that the future peoples

00:03:15.239 --> 00:03:16.440
of the 24th century

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:18.850
won't have supershort attention spans

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:19.850
that prevent them from enjoying

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:20.850
ninety minute movies.

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:21.850
Maybe their touchstones will be

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:22.850
"Charlie Bit My Finger,"

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:25.050
or the cat who likes to jump into boxes.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.050
What do you think

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:27.050
is the most durable story of our time?

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:28.129
Let me know in the comments,

00:03:28.129 --> 00:03:29.580
subscribe to the Wired channel,

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:31.440
and click on my videos over there.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:34.870
With the tiny animatronic versions of me.

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:37.910
What? No, no.

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:39.940
They're animatronic.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:45.060
Look how stiff and jerky their movements are!

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.400
What a thing to say to me!

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:48.900
I bet YOU are animatronic!

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:50.970
Yeah, I thought so.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:52.350
A real human being human

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:53.799
couldn't be that heartless.

